{
  "id": "Compound::DB00846 - Gene::2908",
  "verbalization": "Flurandrenolide appears to interact with Nr3c1 through a shared pathway involving steroid-binding proteins. The evidence suggests that Flurandrenolide binds to Serpina6, which in turn is bound by various glucocorticoids, including Alclometasone, Halobetasol Propionate, and Flumethasone Pivalate. All these compounds are classified as therapeutic glucocorticoids, indicating a common functional category. The lowest common ancestors of Flurandrenolide and these glucocorticoids are linked to the broader category of steroids, suggesting a potential mechanism of action involving steroid receptor modulation. The consistent binding of Flurandrenolide to Serpina6 and its subsequent interaction with Nr3c1 implies that the drug may influence steroid receptor activity through a shared binding site or pathway. This relationship is supported by the presence of multiple glucocorticoid analogs that bind to the same target, reinforcing the hypothesis that Flurandrenolide exerts its effects via a steroid-dependent mechanism.",
